{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Come, let us descend.</b> The speech of HaShem with the angels." "<b>And let us confound.</b> As for the word ונבלה [\"and we will confound\"], all the grammarians say it is in the nifal binyan, and similar to it is ונבקה רוח מצרים (Isaiah 19:3), and likewise אבלה נבלה (ibid. 24:4). This is far-fetched, for what reason would \"let us descend\" and \"let us be confounded\" — their language — [go together]? And their language was not confounded because of the descent. Rather, ונבלה is like ונעשה [\"and let us make\"], and the proof is that He said at the end, כי שם בלל ד' (Genesis 11:9). And this is his grammatical analysis [that it is] from the hifil binyan, and it ought to have been whole, ונבלילה, with doubling of the [middle] root letter; וְנָבֵלָה on the pattern of וְנָסֵבָה את ארון ד' (1 Chronicles 13:3) (and with the doubling missing, ונבלה שם). And the ancients translated well: ואבלה in place of ונבלה. And if it were as the grammarians say, why is the nun missing? And R. Abraham [Ibn Ezra himself] says their hearts were turned to hate one another, and each one invented a language. And some say that He who teaches man knowledge caused them to forget the knowledge of their language. And the correct view in my eyes is that they were scattered from there, and after they were scattered Nimrod ruled over Babylon, and other kings arose, and after many days, with the death of the first generation, the first language was forgotten. And HaShem scattered them, and it was good for them, and so He said, ומלאו את הארץ (Genesis 1:18)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {1 "Resolved וי\"א as 'And R. Abraham [Ibn Ezra himself] says' based on the standard acronym; possibly an external opinion instead. Citation Genesis 1:18 follows the Hebrew verse numbering (1:28 in English numbering)."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:16.364094841Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}